  "summary": "Premium audio (headphones / earbuds / speakers) and watches. Trend data (May 2026): 'Sony wireless noise canceling headphones' is a Breakout query and 'casio men's watch' is rising +250%. Audio buyers are model-specific (WH-1000XM5 ≠ WH-1000XM4) — verify exact model number. Casio G-Shock and vintage A158/F-91W lines are durable resale because the products themselves are quasi-immortal; even 10-year-old G-Shocks sell. Premium watch brands (Seiko, Citizen) hold value especially in their Japanese-domestic-market variants.",
  "field_workflow": [
    "Audio: model number on the headband (e.g. WH-1000XM5 stamped underneath ear cup)",
    "Audio: confirm USB-C charging cable + carrying case included",
    "Watches: case-back engraving identifies model + serial",
    "Watches: original strap and clasp included = +20-30%",
    "Watches: working condition (run a battery test or auto-wind) — non-running watches lose 50%+",
    "Casio G-Shock: backlight + alarm + countdown all functioning"
  ],
  "skip_list": [
    "Replica / fake (Casio especially common)",
    "Counterfeit AirPods / Sony / Bose",
    "Generic Bluetooth headphones",
    "Off-brand Chinese audio",
    "Children's toy watches",
    "Quartz watch dead battery (unless luxury)",
    "Beats Studio Buds (commodity earbuds)",
    "Plantronics Voyager (commercial gear, low resale)"
  ],
